From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:18:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): continuation review fixes: update-gap wait, one
 prepare per session [daveey]

- Worker: a refusal gap past OWNER_WAIT_S checks the board for this attempt's unconsumed checkpoint; the
  hermes update path (restart wait refuses, then the tree moves) never shows a terminal receipt first,
  so without this the worker gave up at OWNER_WAIT_S and the run was reclaimed anyway.
- Owner: prepare() is serialized per session, so a retried kanban.run racing the first cannot append a
  second synthetic result for the same interrupted tool call.
- Drop the _require_admission_open pre-check before prepare (the admission submit already refuses on a
  draining owner; the pre-check only refused earlier with a different error).
- test_core_update_kanban_wait pins the checkpoint the managed Stop booking passes.

Proof: new tests killed by mutants R1 (no board check -> update-gap test fails), R2 (no per-session lock
-> race test writes two tool results), R3 (checkpoint kwargs dropped -> booking test fails).
---
 gateway/session_kanban_continue.py            | 14 ++++-
 hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py            |  5 ++
 tests/gateway/test_core_update_kanban_wait.py |  6 ++-
 .../test_kanban_restart_continuation.py       | 54 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gateway/session_kanban_continue.py b/gateway/session_kanban_continue.py
index 4e59d5c0bd..1cbecd2c8f 100644
--- a/gateway/session_kanban_continue.py
+++ b/gateway/session_kanban_continue.py
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ import logging
 import os
 from pathlib import Path
 import sqlite3
+import threading
 import time
 from typing import NoReturn
 
@@ -42,6 +43,10 @@ CONTINUE_TEXT = (CONTINUE_PREFIX + ' The gateway restarted (a Hermes update) whi
 INTERRUPTED_RESULT = '[interrupted by Hermes update at {at}: re-run if still needed]'
 CONTINUED_EVENT = 'restart_continued'
 REFUSED_EVENT = 'restart_continue_refused'
+# One continuation prepare per session at a time: a retried ``kanban.run`` racing the first must not
+# append a second synthetic result for the same interrupted tool call (prepare runs off the owner loop).
+_PREPARING: dict[str, threading.Lock] = {}
+_PREPARING_GUARD = threading.Lock()
 
 
 def interrupted_result(at) -> str:
@@ -135,10 +140,17 @@ def _answer_interrupted_calls(session_db, session_id, at) -> int:
     return int(session_db._execute_write(write))
 
 
-def prepare(authority, *, principal_id, session_id, context, checkpoint, request_id, owner_db) -> dict:
+def prepare(authority, *, session_id, **kwargs) -> dict:
     """Prove the checkpointed turn can continue in ``session_id``, answer its interrupted tool calls and
     record the continuation as the run's newest ``owner_admitted``. Off the owner loop; raises
     ``RuntimeStoreError(UNSAFE)`` (booked, logged) when continuation cannot be proven safe."""
+    with _PREPARING_GUARD:
+        lock = _PREPARING.setdefault(session_id, threading.Lock())
+    with lock:
+        return _prepare(authority, session_id=session_id, **kwargs)
+
+
+def _prepare(authority, *, principal_id, session_id, context, checkpoint, request_id, owner_db) -> dict:
     if checkpoint.get('unsafe'):
         _refuse(context, checkpoint, checkpoint['unsafe'])
     if checkpoint.get('session_id') != session_id:
diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py
index 63c945d97d..ce5213c479 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_worker_client.py
@@ -202,6 +202,11 @@ async def run(params, board_db):
                     raise OwnerRestartLost(f'Kanban owner did not continue the checkpointed turn: {exc}') from exc
                 raise
             claim.note_refusal(exc)
+            if (claim.silent_for() >= OWNER_WAIT_S and not claim.continuing
+                    and await asyncio.to_thread(_checkpoint, params, board_db, claim) is not None):
+                # [daveey] The stopping owner checkpointed this attempt's turn before the gap (a ``hermes
+                # update`` refuses us in its restart wait, then the tree moves): wait out the restart.
+                claim.continuing = claim.restarted = True
             if claim.silent_for() >= claim.silence_budget():
                 # WebSocket errors can embed remote bodies; only our own messages are quoted.
                 status = getattr(getattr(exc, 'response', None), 'status_code', None)
